</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5df51d8-b812-11f1-9dee-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-224458-225002-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5df51d8-b812-11f1-9dee-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-224458-225002-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb0c2910-b812-11f1-9b9a-e36fb9e8a010</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:55:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Does the future belong to China?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china</link><description>
US President Donald Trump is rolling out the red carpet for his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping ahead of Thursday's summit in Washington. But is China's leader overconfident in thinking the future belongs to Beijing? FRANCE 24's Yinka Oyetade speaks to Rex Li from King's College London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/880eebfa-b80e-11f1-be42-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15234920376ab50f2d4ce053-87492519.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/880eebfa-b80e-11f1-be42-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15234920376ab50f2d4ce053-87492519.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68642b70-b80f-11f1-8f79-6ff327f004b8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:32:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Andrew HILLIAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Massive, maximum destruction’: Putin seeks to bring Ukrainian civilians ‘to their knees’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees</link><description>
Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev from Kyiv, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. According to Zalmayev, Russia’s ongoing attacks on Ukraine reflect a broader political logic in which military force, political objectives and territorial ambitions are intertwined as instruments of Russian strategy. He argues that Moscow’s attacks on civilian infrastructure are designed to exert extreme pressure on Ukrainian society while demonstrating fierce retaliation to domestic audiences in Russia. Zalmayev contrasts this with Ukraine’s strikes on Russian energy infrastructure, which he describes as targeting assets that directly sustain Moscow’s war effort.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab80351e-b80c-11f1-a806-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-203121-203652-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab80351e-b80c-11f1-a806-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-203121-203652-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2a3ce50-b80c-11f1-a30a-ffee22c7666e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:17:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Australia's Medicare AI hack: Its seriousness 'cannot be overstated'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260924-australia-s-medicare-ai-hack-its-seriousness-cannot-be-overstated</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 24: The Spanish press express outrage after the forced eviction of an elderly woman from her Madrid residence. Unrest in the Tigray region sparks fears of a new war between rebels and Ethiopia's central government. Australian authorities reveal that the national health insurance system Medicare was hacked by an AI agent. Finally, we look at Britain's rudest-sounding street names!
