Hundreds of thousands of the faithful and visitors are expected in Paris this weekend as Pope Leo XIV visits the French capital, marking the first papal visit to the country since 2008. France has pulled out all the stops to welcome the pontiff over the two-day visit in the capital and security forces are ensuring maximum protection with some 14,000 police officers, gendarmes, and soldiers mobilized across the capital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6a4c14-b80e-11f1-862a-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-110927-111148-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6a4c14-b80e-11f1-862a-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-110927-111148-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80818974-b80e-11f1-bdeb-79c568ce1872</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:09:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels in 'full-blown' war with govt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-in-full-blown-war-with-govt</link><description>
Tigray rebels in Ethiopia told AFP on Thursday they were in a state of "full-blown war" with the federal government, as heavy artillery attacks were reported in neighbouring states. Tensions have been rising for months between the federal government and the authorities in the northern Tigray state, who fought a devastating civil war in 2020-2022 that killed more than 600,000 people, according to African Union estimates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3f364ce-b80d-11f1-91e1-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-110623-110826-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3f364ce-b80d-11f1-91e1-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-110623-110826-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8915aea-b80d-11f1-a5be-35302b3cf256</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:05:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Australia’s Albanese rebukes OpenAI after government website hacked</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-australia-s-albanese-rebukes-openai-after-government-website-hacked</link><description>
Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said Thursday he was extremely concerned about OpenAI 's breach of an Australian health department website and that the artificial intelligence company took too long to reveal the incident. An OpenAI agent infiltrated the public-facing Medicare Statistics Reporting Service portal on June 18, he said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9c83ace-b80c-11f1-ac41-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-104100-104243-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9c83ace-b80c-11f1-ac41-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-104100-104243-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef3e1b86-b80c-11f1-a96a-27fe2bdb0591</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:02:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Particularly heavy night' of Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-particularly-heavy-night-of-russian-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
