An ancient wall discovered in central Paris was hailed as a "major breakthrough" on Wednesday, as the archaeological find may have settled a long-standing debate about the location of the city's original settlement. A roughly 20-metre (66-foot) wall dating from the Gallo-Roman period was discovered in Paris this summer beneath a hospital on the Ile de la Cite, a stone's throw from Notre Dame Cathedral, the French culture ministry said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06fdd64e-b7fe-11f1-9b37-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-102557-102731-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06fdd64e-b7fe-11f1-9b37-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-102557-102731-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c7dabb2-b7fe-11f1-aeb4-c38fe0950520</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:01:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope's visit to France 'an important moment for the Vatican'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-pope-s-visit-to-france-an-important-moment-for-the-vatican</link><description>
France is gearing up for the arrival of Pope Leo XIV in what will be the first state visit to the country by a pontiff since 2008. Seema Gupta, France 24's correspondent in Rome takes a look at the visit from the Vatican's point of view.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2fb10a6-b7fd-11f1-8060-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101838-102515-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2fb10a6-b7fd-11f1-8060-712f76118fd1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101838-102515-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7b58c02-b7fd-11f1-bcce-816ab75beede</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:58:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Fears of flooding, landslides as Hurricane Polo churns off Mexico coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-fears-of-flooding-landslides-as-hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico-coast</link><description>
Residents of Mexico's Pacific beach towns were preparing for heavy rain and dangerous surf ​on Wednesday ‌as Hurricane Polo, a powerful Category 4 storm, tracked northwestward just ⁠offshore, threatening flooding and mudslides along the country's southwestern coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29c3215a-b7fb-11f1-9c52-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101330-101458-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29c3215a-b7fb-11f1-9c52-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101330-101458-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f0f1d12-b7fb-11f1-b447-5f55784b815d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:53:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘I felt like I'd been tricked’: France probes secret filming of women with smart glasses</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-i-felt-like-i-d-been-tricked-france-probes-secret-filming-of-women-with-smart-glasses</link><description>
It's a trend that first started in the US and is becoming more and more prevalent in France. Women are being filmed in the street without their knowledge, by men wearing smart glasses. The men are earning money by posting the videos online without the consent of their victims. Ellen Gainsford has details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34c0c26c-b7f9-11f1-9cb3-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101032-101215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34c0c26c-b7f9-11f1-9cb3-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-101032-101215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a80d3d6-b7f9-11f1-9336-41dc523fbad2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:47:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump welcomes China's Xi to Washington</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-trump-welcomes-china-s-xi-to-washington</link><description>
US President Donald Trump welcomes Chinese President Xi Jinping to the White House on Thursday for a lavish state summit expected to be heavy on symbolism but light on substance, with both leaders keen to showcase stable ties despite a deep underlying rivalry. Trump greeted Xi on arrival on Wednesday evening, the first time a US president has welcomed a foreign leader at Joint Base Andrews in 11 years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/917c28c6-b7f8-11f1-8b13-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-100722-100934-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/917c28c6-b7f8-11f1-8b13-f161c0c5ea55/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-100722-100934-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96f70cb2-b7f8-11f1-ae8b-b3a254ecfe17</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:46:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>A look back at Tunisia's summer of shortages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-look-back-tunisiassummer-shortages</link><description>
Repeated power and water outages, long queues for bottled water, and poultry farms destroyed by the heat: millions of Tunisians were affected by water and electricity shortages over the summer. Our Observers say this is the result of years of underinvestment. The water shortage eased in late August when authorities sent millions of bottles of water to stores, but many are concerned the same thing could happen next summer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41600610-b7f7-11f1-b86b-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-09-23-17h28m29s012.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41600610-b7f7-11f1-b86b-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-09-23-17h28m29s012.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02480b22-b7fb-11f1-9882-b1e943e503d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:43:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Risk to humanity': At UN, tech leaders urge caution in AI development</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-risk-to-humanity-at-un-tech-leaders-urge-caution-in-ai-development</link><description>
The heads of major artificial intelligence firms pleaded with the United Nations on Wednesday to save the world or at least its people — by somehow regulating the fast-expanding technology that they have been designing. “If managed poorly, I even believe AI could be a risk to humanity as a whole,” said Dario Amodei, chief executive officer of Anthropic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1b5b960-b7f7-11f1-be0b-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-100540-100719-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1b5b960-b7f7-11f1-be0b-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-100540-100719-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6cade4e-b7f7-11f1-a341-bf407ca729b1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:38:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
